    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners` following the existing \"reject\" step pattern, keeping structural impact low \u2014 no existing function was modified, only new small single-method classes were added plus one YAML wiring edit.\n\n**New files:**\n- `function/owner/RejectCrowdedCity.java` \u2014 a one-method step that counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitive, matching `AssignCustomerCode`'s convention) and throws `CrowdedCityException` when the count is \u2265 50.\n- `escalation/CrowdedCityException.java` \u2014 checked exception (mirrors `DuplicateHouseholdException`).\n- `escalation/CrowdedCityExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` (mirrors the household handler).\n- `officefloor/escalation/...CrowdedCityException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Edited:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `rejectCrowdedCity` step between `rejectHousehold` and `build`.\n\nEach new function is a cohesive unit with WMC_other of 0, and no method or class grew. The acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a city to 50, expect the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, as does the full suite.",
